Package: bootsurvimp
Type: Package
Title: Bootstrap Variance Estimation for Imputed Survey Data
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Zeinab", "Mashreghi", email = "z.mashreghi@uwinnipeg.ca",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-0563-0792")),
    person("Sophia", "Perron", role = "aut",
           comment = "Student developer"),
    person("Antonio", "Axalan", role = "aut",
           comment = "Student developer"))
Description: Bootstrap methods for estimating the variance of estimators
    (totals, means and quantiles) computed on imputed survey data under
    stratified sampling designs. Rescaling bootstrap methods cover the
    independent bootstrap of Mashreghi, Leger and Haziza (2014), in its
    rescaled-data and bootstrap-weights forms, the unequal response
    probability bootstrap of Mashreghi and Deng (2023), and the Shao and
    Sitter (1996) method, under mean, random hot-deck, regression and ratio
    imputation. Pseudo-population bootstrap methods cover doubly and
    multiply robust regression and class hot-deck imputation under the
    nonresponse-model, imputation-model and multiply robust schemes of Chen,
    Haziza, Leger and Mashreghi (2019) and Chen, Haziza and Mashreghi (2021).
